**Short, one item.** Follow-up to `plan__ta-anchor-pr2-c10-ksat-effect-arithmetic.md` (`.DONE` — thank
you, the §2e.3 correction in plan tip `62c37c46` is accurate; I re-derived it independently and get
`r = 0.006/0.073 = 0.082192`, `(0.80/0.85)·(0.932192/0.882192) = 0.994521` ⇒ **−0.548%**, matching your
table exactly, including `N_sat`/`ITL_sat`/`μ_sat` at both k values).

**Why this needs to be in the plan and not just my review:** the coder reads Type 3 plan docs for
scope, not review docs. If the bound lives only in `ta-anchor-dynamic-refresh-review.md` I catch the
problem after C10 is written, which costs a fixture rewrite. Same reasoning that made the §2e.3
correction worth raising before the commit existed.

## The gap

Plan §1.1's C10 row asks for a "`KvCacheThreshold: 0.5` fixture asserting PRC tracks config (red:
pinned at 0.85), **tight tolerance**", and §2e.3 restates the red-before-green intent. Neither states
what "tight" means numerically — and the conventional tolerance in the target file is on the wrong side
of the bound.

Numbers, with `A=0.073 B=0.006 KV_max=1024000 KVreq=4600` (the shipped fixture, `analyzer_test.go:259-274`):

| k | `N_sat` | `ITL_sat` | `μ_sat` |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0.85 (today) | 189.2174 | 0.06805 | 2780.56 |
| 0.80 (post-C10 default) | 178.0870 | 0.06440 | 2765.33 |
| **0.50 (the new fixture)** | 111.3043 | 0.04250 | **2618.93** |

The gap the fixture must resolve is `2780.56 / 2618.93 = 1.06172` — **6.17%**. So
`BeNumerically("~", 2618.93, tol)` stays **green at k=0.85** for any relative `tol ≥ 6.17%`.

`analyzer_test.go` uses `BeNumerically("~", muSat, muSat*0.10)` — **±10%** — at all three existing
`TotalSupply` sites (`:367`, `:405`, `:425`). So the single most likely way to write the new fixture,
copying the neighbouring assertion's shape, yields a test that passes before *and* after C10 and pins
nothing. The commit message would claim red-before-green truthfully as intent and falsely as fact, and
neither a green suite nor a diff read would surface it.

## Ask

Add the bound to the §1.1 C10 row and/or §2e.3: expected value **2618.93**, relative tolerance
**< 6.17%**, **±1% recommended** (band `[2592.7, 2645.1]`, excludes 2780.56 with room). One clause is
enough — "tolerance ≤1% relative; ±10% (the idiom elsewhere in this file) leaves the fixture green at
0.85 and must not be copied."

## One thing that is *not* a risk, for calibration

At `k=0.5` the numerator-only error (the 0.9412-class mistake §2e.3 now warns about) would give
`2782.0 × (0.5/0.85) = 1636.5` against a correct 2618.93 — a 60% miss that any sane tolerance catches.
So this fixture is self-protecting against that error and vulnerable only to a loose tolerance. The
`k=0.80` default-config expectations are the exact reverse: immune to looseness (they move 0.55%, far
inside ±10%) and fully exposed to the numerator-only error. Two different traps, one per fixture —
§2e.3 already covers the second; this handoff is only about the first.

